## Install BatchVault

BatchVault needs Python 3.11.4 or later. To get exactly the version that made this archive:

```
pip install "batchvault${extra}==$version"
```

or with pipx or uv$crypto:

```
pipx install "batchvault${extra}==$version"
uv tool install "batchvault${extra}==$version"
```

A newer version normally reads older archives too. Other ways to run it:

- Docker: `ghcr.io/coldsofttech/batchvault:$version`$docker_variant
- GitHub Action: `coldsofttech/BatchVault@v1`
${sevenzip_note}
## Restore the files

$restore_intro

```
batchvault unpack $manifest_arg -o restored$sign_flag$pass_flag
```

The files appear in `restored/`, in the same folders they came from. Every volume and every restored file is checked against its checksum before it is placed there.

To check the archive without restoring it:

```
batchvault verify $manifest_arg$sign_flag$pass_flag
```

### Other ways to restore

`unpack` and `verify` accept any of these in place of the manifest:

- a folder: `batchvault unpack . -o restored`
${one_volume}- a list of volumes or manifests, one path per line: `batchvault unpack volumes.txt -o restored`

Add `--public-key` to check a signature and `--password-file` for an encrypted archive. Run `batchvault unpack --help` for everything else.
